<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khafre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">26th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/26th-century-bce">26th century BCE</a> · Also known as Chephren</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khafre was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s Fourth Dynasty in the 26th century BCE and a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khufu">Khufu</a>. He built the second pyramid at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giza">Giza</a>, and the Great Sphinx is generally attributed to his reign. His diorite seated statue from his valley temple is one of the masterpieces of Old Kingdom sculpture.</p></div>
